menu "Example Configuration"

    config ENABLE_ULTRAWIDELOCK_BLE_UWB
        bool "Enable the credential protocol (Apple Home Key) over BLE + UWB"
        default y
        help
            Advertise the Door Lock cluster's credential Provisioning + BLE-UWB
            features and register the credential reader delegate, so Apple Home can
            provision an Express (BLE + UWB) Home Key into Wallet for this reader.

    config ENABLE_HA_MQTT
        bool "Publish distance and access events to Home Assistant over MQTT"
        default n
        depends on ENABLE_ULTRAWIDELOCK_BLE_UWB
        select ULTRAWIDELOCK_CRED_ACCESS_LISTENER
        help
            Publish UWB distance and credential access verdicts straight to a TLS
            MQTT broker, on the topics MQTT Discovery expects, so Home
            Assistant builds the device
            through MQTT Discovery with no host-side agent running. Lock
            control stays on Matter; this carries only what Matter does not
            expose.

            Off by default: it adds esp-mqtt and a TLS session to the image,
            and it is useless until a broker is provisioned. Nothing about a
            broker is compiled in — host, port, login, CA certificate and node
            name are runtime NVS config, set with the `hamqtt` console command.

            Do not set this on its own. Build with `make build HAMQTT=1`, which
            also applies the mbedTLS record sizing in
            sdkconfig.defaults.hamqtt; without it mbedtls_ssl_setup cannot get
            a contiguous 16 KiB input record next to Matter, NimBLE and Wi-Fi,
            and every connection fails with -0x7F00 before the handshake.

    menu "Two-anchor inside/outside gate"

        config ULTRAWIDELOCK_ANCHOR_BASELINE_MM
            int "Anchor separation, mm (role 1)"
            default 0
            help
                Distance between this lock and the second anchor. MEASURE IT at
                install; it is not derivable and every triangle test is sized
                from it. 0 means no satellite mounted, which leaves the verdict
                UNKNOWN and the door behaving exactly as a single-anchor lock.

                `sat_baseline <mm>` overwrites this at runtime and persists it,
                which is how the bench calibrates.

        config ULTRAWIDELOCK_ANCHOR_BASELINE_2_MM
            int "Anchor separation, mm (role 2)"
            default 0

        config ULTRAWIDELOCK_ANCHOR_BASELINE_3_MM
            int "Anchor separation, mm (role 3)"
            default 0

        config ULTRAWIDELOCK_ANCHOR_TOL_MM
            int "Triangle-inequality slack, mm"
            default 300
            help
                Size at 3 sigma of the measured per-link jitter: this gate
                catches impossible geometry, not ordinary noise. Too tight and
                every legitimate pair is rejected, which reads on a bench as a
                dead satellite rather than a misconfiguration.

        config ULTRAWIDELOCK_ANCHOR_DEADBAND_MM
            int "Half-width of the UNKNOWN band about the boundary, mm"
            default 150
            help
                Size at about 2 sigma. Within it the two distances are not far
                enough apart for their difference to have a reliable sign, and
                saying UNKNOWN beats guessing -- a phone in the doorway is
                genuinely ambiguous and should read that way.

        config ULTRAWIDELOCK_ANCHOR_BOUNDARY_BIAS_MM
            int "Shift of the side boundary toward the inside anchor, mm"
            default 0
            help
                0 keeps the boundary on the perpendicular bisector, which is the
                door plane when the anchors straddle the door -- the shipping
                install. A positive value is for a bench where both anchors sit
                on the same side of the walkway.

                IT MUST STAY SEVERAL SIGMA BELOW THE BASELINE. At bias ==
                baseline the INSIDE locus degenerates and noise decides every
                verdict.

        config ULTRAWIDELOCK_ANCHOR_STALE_MS
            int "How long a peer report stays usable, ms"
            default 1500
            help
                Past this, the satellite's distance is no longer evidence about
                where the phone is now. Expiry yields UNKNOWN, which permits --
                absence is not evidence of insideness.

        config ULTRAWIDELOCK_ANCHOR_SELF_INSIDE
            bool "This lock is the INSIDE anchor"
            default n
            help
                Which side of the door THIS board is on. A MOUNTING FACT: it
                fails no test and crashes nothing when wrong, it silently
                inverts the side verdict.

    endmenu

endmenu
